<div id="body" class="mktoText" style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, Sans-Serif; padding:10px;"> 
<p>Hi {{lead.First Name:default=Friend}},</p> 
<div>
You understand how challenging it can be to satisfy customers in other parts of the world, especially when it comes to payments. 
<br />
<br /> The transaction and handling of payments from one country to another involves a complex FX landscape. Even your 
<a href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/an-introduction-to-cross-border-invoicing-and-business-payments?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email" target="_blank" id="">invoicing</a> may have local regulations governing what an invoice must look like and the method of delivery. 
<br />
<br /> Flywire’s latest industry research shows that 95% of your peers believe that if they could deal with exchange rates in an easier way, they would increase their global expansion efforts.
<br />
<br /> If you start invoicing your payers with local options, compliant presentations, and a top-notch payment experience, you can guarantee timely international payments and reduced DSO. We put together 
<a href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/an-introduction-to-cross-border-invoicing-and-business-payments?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email" target="_blank" id="">5 steps to invoicing international customers</a> and the considerations your team should make in building out a cross-border payments capability. 
<br />
<br />Let me know if this was helpful, I would be happy to provide other resources for you and your team,
<br />
<br /> Josh Easterly
</div> 
<div>
<br />
</div> 
</div>  
